invariant: INV-59
file: mldsa.c
catches: test/wycheproof.sh
reason: entry A[i][j] is sampled from rho || i || j, where FIPS 204
  Algorithm 32 gives rho || j || i, so A is another matrix and no honest
  signature verifies. bin/mldsa_test cannot see it, because its
  signatures have z = 0 and A z is 0 for every A. Wycheproof's valid cases
  fail.

--- old
        if (!mld_sample_ntt(&entry, pk, (uint8_t)j, (uint8_t)i)) {
--- new
        if (!mld_sample_ntt(&entry, pk, (uint8_t)i, (uint8_t)j)) {
